===============================================================================
1. Prerequisites:
===============================================================================

Please follow instructions in the apps/sample_apps/deepstream-app/README on how
to install the prerequisites for Deepstream SDK, the DeepStream SDK itself and
the apps.

The Python probe modules must be installed at:
  /opt/nvidia/deepstream/deepstream/service-maker/modules/python/

===============================================================================
2. Purpose:
===============================================================================

This document describes the sample deepstream_python_probe application.

It demonstrates how to use an installed Python probe module with the
DeepStream service-maker pipeline API. Python probes are lightweight handlers
written in Python that can be attached to pipeline elements as glue logic —
for example to overlay OSD annotations or transform metadata between elements.

The sample uses the "sample_video_probe" Python probe module which counts
vehicles and persons per frame and overlays the result on the OSD.

The Python probe module is discovered and registered in CommonFactory by
importing it at application startup. Once registered, it can be attached to
pipeline elements by name string — identically to a compiled C++ probe plugin:

  - YAML config:  type: python.sample_video_probe
  - Direct API:   pipeline.attach("infer", "sample_video_probe", "svp",
                                  properties={"font-size": 18})

===============================================================================
3. Usage:
===============================================================================

  Run with the h264 elementary stream or YAML pipeline config file.
  With YAML pipeline config approach, user can modify the config file to
  configure pipeline and probe properties.

    $ python3 deepstream_python_probe.py <h264_elementary_stream>

    Or

    $ python3 deepstream_python_probe.py <pipeline config in yaml>

  To enable end-to-end latency measurement with the measure_latency_probe
  module, set the following environment variable before running:

    $ export NVDS_ENABLE_LATENCY_MEASUREMENT=1

  Note: with RTSP/live sources, both measure_fps_probe and
  measure_latency_probe report valid values (FPS and latency respectively).

===============================================================================
4. Reusable Python Probe Modules:
===============================================================================

  Additional Python probe modules (measure_fps_probe, measure_latency_probe,
  kitti_dump_probe, add_message_meta_probe, resnet_tensor_parser) are
  pre-installed alongside sample_video_probe. Each can be used the same way —
  import to register, then attach by name in YAML or the direct API.

  For the full list of modules and their parameters see:
    /opt/nvidia/deepstream/deepstream/service-maker/modules/python/README
